---
// Terms of use. Standard terms for a free, static, device-side toolbox: free, provided as is,
// runs on your device, no warranty. Draft text for Atharva to review; keep it in step with
// /privacy/ (analytics, storage) and /about/ (what the site is).
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { generatePageTitle } from '@lib/titles';
import { withBase } from '@lib/paths';

const description =
  'ToyTools is free to use, runs on your device and is provided as is, with no warranty. These are the terms that come with that.';

const updated = '28 October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={generatePageTitle('terms')} description={description} maxWidth="tool">
  <article class="page-doc">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">{description}</p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>ToyTools is free. There is no account, no subscription and nothing to sign up for.</li>
      <li>The tools run on your device. What you type or open stays in your browser, as the <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>Privacy</a> page explains.</li>
      <li>Everything is provided as is, with no warranty. Check results that matter before you rely on them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Using the tools</h2>
    <p>
      You may use ToyTools for personal, educational or work purposes, free of charge. Please do
      not use it to break the law, to harm other people, or to disrupt the site, for example by
      overloading it with automated requests.
    </p>

    <h2>Runs on your device</h2>
    <p>
      ToyTools is a static site. Each tool's code is downloaded to your browser and the work
      happens there. Anything a tool saves for you is kept in your browser's storage on that
      device, and you can export or delete it from <a href={withBase('/settings/')}>Settings</a>.
      You are responsible for keeping your own copies of anything you need.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      ToyTools is provided as is and as available, without warranties of any kind, express or
      implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy and availability. Tools can have
      bugs, rounding differences or outdated rules, and the site can change or go offline at any
      time.
    </p>
    <p>
      Calculators for money, health, dates and similar topics give estimates for information only.
      They are not financial, medical, legal or other professional advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, ToyTools and its maker are not liable for any loss or damage
      that comes from using, or being unable to use, the site or its results.
    </p>

    <h2>Content and links</h2>
    <p>
      The site's code, text and design belong to ToyTools unless a page or a credit says otherwise.
      Third-party libraries are used under their own licences. Links to other sites are given for
      convenience, and ToyTools is not responsible for their content.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated as the site changes. The date above shows the latest version, and
      the <a href={withBase('/changelog/')}>Changelog</a> records notable changes.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms, or anything else, go through
      <a href={withBase('/feedback/')}>Contact and feedback</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
